WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:26.910
We're still finding out details about this
just unconscionable tragedy that took place

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.810
in Beirut, Lebanon, a couple of days ago.

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:32.840
But we do now know enough that we can at least
say a few things.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:40.780
On Tuesday, there was an absolutely gigantic
explosion in Beirut, Lebanon, at warehouses

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:44.340
that stored highly explosive materials.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:48.850
And the video of this explosion looks the
way that nuclear weapons are often portrayed

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:50.930
in Hollywood films.

00:00:50.930 --> 00:00:58.690
And it was, in fact, one of the largest explosions
essentially in the history of humanity.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:02.530
Shock waves smashed homes and ripped off building
facades.

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:06.360
And so far, the death toll is at 157.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.160
Now, just yesterday, it was at 113.

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:10.610
So it's climbing rapidly.

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:13.830
There's another 80 people currently unaccounted
for.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:19.220
Ominously, and more than 5000 people have
been injured, but that those those numbers

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:22.730
are probably a fraction of what ultimately
is going to be uncovered.

00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:32.480
Tragically, the shockwave spread so far that
300000 people were left without homes because

00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:38.950
even miles away, the impacts of this explosion
were felt now very early in the process of

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:42.160
trying to figure out what happened on Tuesday.

00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:45.810
Donald Trump wildly talked about this as an
attack.

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:47.660
He said it looked like a bomb.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:53.210
And to be very clear, the reason I didn't
report about this yesterday is I knew Trump

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:55.790
had made those assertions with no evidence.

00:01:55.790 --> 00:02:00.270
And I didn't want to fall into a similar type
of speculation.

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:06.380
And in fact, now, two days after the event,
it appears that what Donald Trump floated

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:07.380
was completely wrong.

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:10.250
Now, I'll talk a little bit more later about
him doubling down on that.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:19.030
But to focus on what we do know, this appears
to have been close to 3000 tons of ammonium

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:24.940
nitrate, which can be used in fertilizers
and in bombs, which was stored for years at

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:28.480
the port in Beirut, Lebanon, after being seized.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:32.950
Now, it was stored incorrectly, it appears,
without the proper safety measures.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:39.329
And so far, it looks like inaction and negligence
are to blame for the explosion.

00:02:39.329 --> 00:02:43.560
The words terrorism, attack, bomb are not
being used.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:47.120
And from what we know so far, it was very
irresponsible for Donald Trump to use those

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:48.120
words.

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:53.269
There are reports that what triggered the
explosion was maybe related to construction

00:02:53.269 --> 00:02:56.010
or repair work being done at a warehouse.

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:58.760
It's still early and even that has not yet
been confirmed.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:03.249
And it is believed that these explosive materials
had actually been sitting there for somewhere

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:05.350
in the range of six to seven years.

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:11.999
So right at the blast site, it's complete
devastation and death in a sort of one mile

00:03:11.999 --> 00:03:13.420
radius area.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:19.799
There are partial and full building collapses
and many, many injuries in a two plus mile

00:03:19.799 --> 00:03:21.249
radius from the blast.

00:03:21.249 --> 00:03:24.939
You start to go in the direction of windows
blown out damage to buildings.

00:03:24.939 --> 00:03:27.420
More on the injury side again.

00:03:27.420 --> 00:03:32.520
And there are damaged buildings all the way
out to six miles from the blast, if you can

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:33.520
imagine.

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.280
So this is now a full blown disaster.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:36.890
So it's a disaster zone.

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:38.510
It's a catastrophe.

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:41.150
Humanitarian groups are trying to get into
the area to provide help.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:45.620
Other nonprofits and of course, everything
is in the context of coronavirus.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:50.060
And that is significantly compounding the
difficulty.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:56.510
When you have a raging pandemic, any kind
of humanitarian mission becomes more more

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:57.549
difficult.

00:03:57.549 --> 00:04:02.609
And again, the blast is considered to be about
20 percent of the size of Hiroshima.

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:06.749
I mean, just think about the magnitude of
that.

00:04:06.749 --> 00:04:16.669
Now, again, there is almost no important global
news story in 2020 in which our president

00:04:16.669 --> 00:04:19.389
does not become a reckless participant.

00:04:19.389 --> 00:04:26.330
And case in point, calling this an attack
early floating the idea of a bomb was completely

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:27.330
irresponsible.

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:32.110
At first it seemed maybe he was leaking information
from a classified briefing he had received.

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:35.740
Maybe he knew something that had not yet been
made public.

00:04:35.740 --> 00:04:36.740
He didn't.

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:41.050
He was just wildly speculating, again, showing
that there's a level of irresponsibility that

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:43.920
he just can't get away from as president of
the United States.

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:46.470
And I'm going to talk more later about Trump
doubling down on it.

00:04:46.470 --> 00:04:50.060
But instantly you have right wingers posting
everywhere on the Internet.

00:04:50.060 --> 00:04:52.970
It is an attack because of what Donald Trump
said.

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:59.590
The reality is that we probably still don't
know the whole story, but that type of speculation

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:02.650
from a president is childishly irresponsible.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:06.980
And in fact, there is a long list of ammonium
nitrate explosions, including here in the

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:12.420
United States, that you might even remember
in 2013, there was an ammonium nitrate explosion

00:05:12.420 --> 00:05:18.230
in west Texas, which also led to speculation
about terrorism and attacks and bombs.

00:05:18.230 --> 00:05:19.230
That's not what it was.

00:05:19.230 --> 00:05:20.600
15 people did die.

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:23.110
So there can always be foul play.

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:27.760
This is not an out of the world unbelievable
situation as it's been reported and Trump's

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:31.871
ignorance and irrational speculation, as always,
causing more problems once again.

